---
import Container from "../Container.astro";
import SectionHeading from "../SectionHeading.astro";
import FAQItem from "../FAQItem.astro";
---

<Container>
	<SectionHeading title="FAQ" id="faq" />
	<div class="divide-y divide-solarized-base2 mt-6">
		<FAQItem question="Which group should I pick?">
			<p>
				If you're curious and want to try it, take the open group. If you already know you want this
				to be a regular part of your life for a while, apply for the closed one. You can do both —
				they meet on alternating weeks.
			</p>
		</FAQItem>
		<FAQItem question="Do I have to share personal things?">
			<p>
				No. Share what feels right in the moment, and nothing beyond that. Openness usually happens on
				its own once a group feels safe, and it doesn't need to be pushed.
			</p>
		</FAQItem>
		<FAQItem question="What if I don't know what to say?">
			<p>
				Then say that. "I don't know what to say" is a real answer, and often a more interesting one
				than something prepared. Simply remaining silent is also always an option.
			</p>
		</FAQItem>
    <FAQItem question="Can I keep my camera turned off during a session?">
			<p>
				During a session, we strongly encourage everyone to have their camera turned on. We are practicing connecting with other people and being able to see each other is fundamental to this. That being said, if you have technical difficulties or need to shortly step away, you can of course always turn off your camera temporarily.
			</p>
		</FAQItem>
		<FAQItem question="Do I need to meditate, or be into any of this?">
			<p>No. Sitting quietly for a few minutes is just a way of arriving, no prerequisites required.</p>
		</FAQItem>
		<FAQItem question="Can I listen without taking part?">
			<p>
				Not really — there's no audience here, only participants. But you can pass on anything you
				don't want to do, and listening is already half the practice.
			</p>
		</FAQItem>
		<FAQItem question="What's in the application?">
			<p>
				A few short questions about you and what brings you here. It's not a test, and I'm not looking
				for experience. It mostly helps me see whether the group will work for you and whether the
				timing fits.
			</p>
		</FAQItem>
		<FAQItem question="What if I miss a session in the closed group?">
			<p>
				That's fine, it happens. Just let the group know. If it turns out you can't make most of them,
				we'll talk about it.
			</p>
		</FAQItem>
		<FAQItem question="What happens when a cycle ends?">
			<p>
				A new one starts, and you can join again if you want. The open group keeps running throughout
				either way.
			</p>
		</FAQItem>
		<FAQItem question="What does it cost?">
			<p>
				The open group is free. The closed group carries a support contribution of €25–100 for
				the cycle — entirely optional, and separate from applying. See
				<a href="/support">Support</a> for how to chip in.
			</p>
		</FAQItem>
	</div>
</Container>
